+
+Three separate internal-publication rows list one container each. **LTI-0237-2016-0012** under Fort Worth covers **1/1/2001-12/31/2004**. **LTI-0237-2017-0004** under Boston covers **9/30/2001-9/30/2006**. **LTI-0237-2017-0023** under College Park covers **1/1/2006-12/31/2006**. These are leads to period guidance. Their series descriptions leave case-specific correspondence and contents open. Two boundaries are preserved: the previously identified directives accession **LTI-0237-2018-0020** begins in September 1987 and the internal-publication accession **LTI-0237-2018-0023** covers calendar 2002. [FY2016 Q2](https://www.archives.gov/research/accessions/2016-quarter-2) · [FY2017 Q4](https://www.archives.gov/research/accessions/2017-quarter-4) · [FY2018 Q3](https://www.archives.gov/research/accessions/2018-quarter-3)
+
+## Distinct series and access observations
+
+The 2022 Fort Worth relocation notice separately lists **NAID 2723191**, *Directives Case Files*, **1979-1995**, from the Mike Monroney Aeronautical Center, Management Analysis Division. The College Park accession **LTI-0237-2016-0027** gives the similar title and dates **1/1/1979-2/28/1995**. The relocation notice gives neither that accession ID nor an accession-to-series crosswalk. Preserve both location/date descriptions separately. The notice also lists **NAID 241990398**, *Organizational Planning Files*, **2006-2008**, from the Southwest Region Program Evaluation Office. That record creator and series title bound its possible relevance to delegated authority. The notice describes a planned transfer to Kansas City with estimated availability dates. Actual arrival and present box location remain unverified. [Relocation notice](https://www.archives.gov/fort-worth/2022-fortworth-records-move) · [Catalog link 2723191](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/2723191) · [Catalog link 241990398](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/241990398)
+
+Web retrieval reported **Cache miss** for each catalog link. Direct HTTP separately returned **200**, **text/html**, and identical **5,454-byte** entities at both links. The saved HTML has an empty app root, seven script tags and neither target series title. The matching digest applies to those response bodies. The catalog descriptions and folder listings were unavailable in those retrievals. [Access results](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+## Which record to look for
+
+- **NC1-237-77-03, item 2, physical pp. 8–9.** The directive case file description includes the issued directive, clearance and approvals, and significant background. The annotated form preserves the typed **“long term or permanent material”** phrase struck through and the handwritten **“Arranged numerically”** note. On the continuation, the typed **“four years or earlier”** is struck through alongside handwritten **“no more than 4 yrs. old”**. Keep those variants tied to the image. The cover’s item 2 status is **“P (Active)”** as of **06/26/2026**, subject to its qualification about subsequent supersession. The body and item status give a records-classification lead. A specific accession or transfer requires its own inventory or receipt. [Status sheet](https://www.archives.gov/files/records-mgmt/rcs/schedules/departments/department-of-transportation/rg-0237/nc1-237-77-03_sf115.pdf#page=1) · [Item 2](https://www.archives.gov/files/records-mgmt/rcs/schedules/departments/department-of-transportation/rg-0237/nc1-237-77-03_sf115.pdf#page=8)
+- **NC-174-000124, physical pp. 1–2 and 5.** The accounting and GAO audit schedule’s narrative refers to **“Job NN 169-45”** and to retained directive case files. The reproduced older directive form on p. 5 separates the broadly applicable policy class, with **“RETAIN”**, from temporary directives, with **“AFTER 5 YEARS”** in the inactive-file disposal clause. The 2023 status sheet marks the accounting and GAO schedule inactive and lists replacement items under **N1-237-09-023**. Keep the attachment, the supersession of the main schedule items, and NC1-237-77-03 item 2’s separate status distinct. No GAO audit category is assigned to the 2006 OIG case here. [Status and accounting schedule](https://www.archives.gov/files/records-mgmt/rcs/schedules/departments/department-of-transportation/rg-0237/nc-174-000124_sf115.pdf#page=1) · [Older attachment](https://www.archives.gov/files/records-mgmt/rcs/schedules/departments/department-of-transportation/rg-0237/nc-174-000124_sf115.pdf#page=5)
+
+**Next test.** Check a dated folder list or transfer manifest for the exact order number **1360.16**, July 12, 1985, and historical office **APF-100**. A matching folder can then be inspected for the issued manual, amendments and clearance or distribution records. For later internal guidance, identify the exact edition and its relationship to the 2006 policy. The actual corrected May 2003 answer and recipient acknowledgment, signed FAA action or no-action decision, OIG recommendation-specific outcomes, and their case-level routing remain separate TODOs. A title or date overlap alone leaves those links untested. [Earlier correspondence policy and locator](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/7dcb6c28f8c4496148f11406570140b3c18e9eda/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-correspondence-predecessor-and-mail-controls-2026-11-08/README.md) · [OIG report, pp. 12–13](https://www.oig.dot.gov/sites/default/files/cc2006085.pdf#page=12)
+
